Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:16:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sidebar): a window on another gateway still lists this
 Mac's own chats live [daveey]

The sidebar list follows the window's connection. With the window on the hub,
$sessions held only hub rows, so mergeOfflineFallback judged this Mac's backend
silent and re-added the boot-snapshot copies of every local chat: frozen at
launch, no cron_active / kanban_* / outcome stamps. They shadow the stamped
projects-tree rows, so chats owning a live cron job showed no stripe instead of
periodic (session audit 2026-10-29 20:00 PDT: 20261026_205117_f67f0d,
20261029_140918_f8947c; renderer rows carried offline_synced_at from the 19:22
launch, the tree row carried cron_active: true).

refreshSessions now also lists the primary's recents (pinned included) when the
window's connection is not the primary, tags them with the primary's id and
folds them into the page. A failed primary read leaves the window's page as is.
